/* ============================================================================
complex-argument.epher -- arg(z) in radians and degrees

arg(z) is the angle of z from the positive real axis, in (-pi, pi]
(Churchill and Brown, "Complex Variables and Applications", sec. 1, 7).
The built-in arg gives radians; deg converts to degrees. The four
diagonal directions come out at the exact multiples 45, 135, -135 and
-90 degrees, and 3 + 4i at arctan(4/3) = 53.1301023542 degrees. The
radian values are floats accurate to about 12 digits.

Run it from a terminal:
  Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/algebra/complex/complex-argument.epher
  Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\algebra\complex\complex-argument.epher"
  macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/algebra/complex/complex-argument.epher

No knobs to edit; the values below are fixed examples.
============================================================================ */

// ---- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
print("arg(1 + i):", arg(1 + i))
print("in degrees:", deg(arg(1 + i)))
print("arg(-1 + i):", arg(-1 + i))
print("in degrees:", deg(arg(-1 + i)))
print("arg(-1 - i):", arg(-1 - i))
print("in degrees:", deg(arg(-1 - i)))
print("arg(-i):", arg(-i))
print("in degrees:", deg(arg(-i)))
print("arg(3 + 4i):", arg(3 + 4i))
print("in degrees:", deg(arg(3 + 4i)))
/* ---- expected output ----
= arg(1 + i): 0.785398163397
= in degrees: 45
= arg(-1 + i): 2.35619449019
= in degrees: 135
= arg(-1 - i): -2.35619449019
= in degrees: -135
= arg(-i): -1.57079632679
= in degrees: -90
= arg(3 + 4i): 0.927295218002
= in degrees: 53.1301023542
*/
